    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "•\nThere is to be an Australian Border Force Commissioner of\nthe Australian Border Force.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner has the control of\nthe operations of the Australian Border Force.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner and APS\nemployees in the Australian Border Force are able to exercise\npowers under the Customs Act 1901, the Migration Act 1958,\nthe Maritime Powers Act 2013 and other Commonwealth\nlaws.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner is also known as\nthe Comptroller-General of Customs.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner may give\ndirections to Immigration and Border Protection workers to do\nwith the administration and control of the operations of the\nAustralian Border Force or the performance of functions or\nexercise of powers by such workers under a law of the\nCommonwealth.\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nOffice and role of the Australian Border Force Commissioner  Division 2\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "•\nThere is to be an Australian Border Force Commissioner of\nthe Australian Border Force.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner has the control of\nthe operations of the Australian Border Force.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner and APS\nemployees in the Australian Border Force are able to exercise\npowers under the Customs Act 1901, the Migration Act 1958,\nthe Maritime Powers Act 2013 and other Commonwealth\nlaws.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner is also known as\nthe Comptroller-General of Customs.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner may give\ndirections to Immigration and Border Protection workers to do\nwith the administration and control of the operations of the\nAustralian Border Force or the performance of functions or\nexercise of powers by such workers under a law of the\nCommonwealth.\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nOffice and role of the Australian Border Force Commissioner  Division 2\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d07bfae6527c964903af3c0ad96824346fb7d6a2d001a33acb12743865e771b4",
      "skos:note": "The Australian Border Force Commissioner has control over the operations of the Australian Border Force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "•\nThere is to be an Australian Border Force Commissioner of\nthe Australian Border Force.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner has the control of\nthe operations of the Australian Border Force.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner and APS\nemployees in the Australian Border Force are able to exercise\npowers under the Customs Act 1901, the Migration Act 1958,\nthe Maritime Powers Act 2013 and other Commonwealth\nlaws.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner is also known as\nthe Comptroller-General of Customs.\n•\nThe Australian Border Force Commissioner may give\ndirections to Immigration and Border Protection workers to do\nwith the administration and control of the operations of the\nAustralian Border Force or the performance of functions or\nexercise of powers by such workers under a law of the\nCommonwealth.\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nOffice and role of the Australian Border Force Commissioner  Division 2\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-8-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-8"
      },
