    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Acting Australian Border Force Commissioner",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\nthe Australian Border Force Commissioner:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the Australian Border Force\nCommissioner (whether or not an appointment has previously\nbeen made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Australian\nBorder Force Commissioner:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nSections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 have rules\nthat apply to acting appointments.\nComptroller-General of Customs\n\n(2) A person appointed to act as the Australian Border Force\nCommissioner is taken, while the person is so acting, to also be the\nComptroller-General of Customs.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\nthe Australian Border Force Commissioner:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the Australian Border Force\nCommissioner (whether or not an appointment has previously\nbeen made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Australian\nBorder Force Commissioner:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nSections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 have rules\nthat apply to acting appointments.\nComptroller-General of Customs\n\n(2) A person appointed to act as the Australian Border Force\nCommissioner is taken, while the person is so acting, to also be the\nComptroller-General of Customs.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-14-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-14-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "831e00306e4b0521923fc132c64c9aa2aed2046e925dada3765cfce9eaee7f1a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Acting Australian Border Force Commissioner",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\nthe Australian Border Force Commissioner:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the Australian Border Force\nCommissioner (whether or not an appointment has previously\nbeen made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Australian\nBorder Force Commissioner:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nSections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 have rules\nthat apply to acting appointments.\nComptroller-General of Customs\n\n(2) A person appointed to act as the Australian Border Force\nCommissioner is taken, while the person is so acting, to also be the\nComptroller-General of Customs."
    },
