    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Suspension or termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may suspend or terminate the appointment\nof the Australian Border Force Commissioner:\n\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n\n(b) if the Commissioner is unable to perform the duties of his or\nher office because of physical or mental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Governor-General may suspend or terminate the appointment\nof the Australian Border Force Commissioner if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) takes steps to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with one or more of his or her creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the\nbenefit of one or more of his or her creditors; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner is absent, except on leave of absence, for\n14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may suspend or terminate the appointment\nof the Australian Border Force Commissioner:\n\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n\n(b) if the Commissioner is unable to perform the duties of his or\nher office because of physical or mental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Governor-General may suspend or terminate the appointment\nof the Australian Border Force Commissioner if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) takes steps to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with one or more of his or her creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the\nbenefit of one or more of his or her creditors; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner is absent, except on leave of absence, for\n14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-21-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-21-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fe7e68eb5012fc1bbe03d5ead8f05f26192e6d3b122b78ada642e176f3b5ae4f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Suspension or termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may suspend or terminate the appointment\nof the Australian Border Force Commissioner:\n\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n\n(b) if the Commissioner is unable to perform the duties of his or\nher office because of physical or mental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Governor-General may suspend or terminate the appointment\nof the Australian Border Force Commissioner if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) takes steps to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with one or more of his or her creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the\nbenefit of one or more of his or her creditors; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner is absent, except on leave of absence, for\n14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or"
    },
