    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing,\ndelegate any of his or her functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth to the following:\n\n(a) the Secretary;\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n(c) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to:\n\n(a) section 30 (resignation in anticipation of termination of\nemployment); or\n\n(b) section 32 (termination of employment for serious\nmisconduct).\nDirections to delegates\n\n(3) An Immigration and Border Protection worker must, in performing\nfunctions or exercising powers under a delegation under\nsubsection (1), comply with any written directions of the\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner.\nSubdelegation by Secretary\n\n(4) If the Secretary is delegated functions or powers under\nsubsection (1), the Secretary may, by writing, delegate any of those\nfunctions or powers to any Immigration and Border Protection\nworker.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing,\ndelegate any of his or her functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth to the following:\n\n(a) the Secretary;\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n(c) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to:\n\n(a) section 30 (resignation in anticipation of termination of\nemployment); or\n\n(b) section 32 (termination of employment for serious\nmisconduct).\nDirections to delegates\n\n(3) An Immigration and Border Protection worker must, in performing\nfunctions or exercising powers under a delegation under\nsubsection (1), comply with any written directions of the\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner.\nSubdelegation by Secretary\n\n(4) If the Secretary is delegated functions or powers under\nsubsection (1), the Secretary may, by writing, delegate any of those\nfunctions or powers to any Immigration and Border Protection\nworker.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "98f6747ae3d699375661760d89cb4ab6d7da3beb4688d222f8b2eaee126cb81f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Delegation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing,\ndelegate any of his or her functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth to the following:\n\n(a) the Secretary;\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n(c) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to:\n\n(a) section 30 (resignation in anticipation of termination of\nemployment); or\n\n(b) section 32 (termination of employment for serious\nmisconduct).\nDirections to delegates\n\n(3) An Immigration and Border Protection worker must, in performing\nfunctions or exercising powers under a delegation under\nsubsection (1), comply with any written directions of the\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner.\nSubdelegation by Secretary\n\n(4) If the Secretary is delegated functions or powers under\nsubsection (1), the Secretary may, by writing, delegate any of those\nfunctions or powers to any Immigration and Border Protection\nworker."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25(1) Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-25-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing,\ndelegate any of his or her functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth to the following:\n\n(a) the Secretary;\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n(c) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing,\ndelegate any of his or her functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth to the following:\n\n(a) the Secretary;\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n(c) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-25-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a6c62cc64eb5d8767da70b8382ff5d8d564cb39af21bcdf92dbe5c768b706728",
      "skos:note": "Delegation of functions or powers to the Secretary and others"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-25-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25(1) Delegation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing,\ndelegate any of his or her functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth to the following:\n\n(a) the Secretary;\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n(c) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce."
    },
