    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-26-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26(2) Directions—administration and control of the operations of the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-26-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), directions under that subsection\nmay relate to the essential qualifications for persons mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(a) or (b) for performing their duties.\nNote 1:\nSee section 23 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the reduction in the\nclassification of an APS employee in the Department if the employee\nlacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for performing his or her\nduties.\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nDelegation and directions  Division 7\n\nSection 26\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote 2:\nSee section 29 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the termination of\nthe employment of an APS employee in the Department if the\nemployee lacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for performing\nhis or her duties.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), directions under that subsection\nmay relate to the essential qualifications for persons mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(a) or (b) for performing their duties.\nNote 1:\nSee section 23 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the reduction in the\nclassification of an APS employee in the Department if the employee\nlacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for performing his or her\nduties.\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nDelegation and directions  Division 7\n\nSection 26\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote 2:\nSee section 29 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the termination of\nthe employment of an APS employee in the Department if the\nemployee lacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for performing\nhis or her duties.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-26-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-26-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f47403f93b148a6c89aabffaf98592e5a7cf34d7242577109915e904a7814ee",
      "skos:note": "Directions under subsection (1) may relate to essential qualifications for persons performing their duties."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-26-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26(2) Directions—administration and control of the operations of the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), directions under that subsection\nmay relate to the essential qualifications for persons mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(a) or (b) for performing their duties.\nNote 1:\nSee section 23 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the reduction in the\nclassification of an APS employee in the Department if the employee\nlacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for performing his or her\nduties.\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nDelegation and directions  Division 7\n\nSection 26\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote 2:\nSee section 29 of the Public Service Act 1999 for the termination of\nthe employment of an APS employee in the Department if the\nemployee lacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for performing\nhis or her duties."
    },
    {
