      "skos:note": "A direction under this section is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-26-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26(6) Directions—administration and control of the operations of the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(6) A direction under this section is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-26-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-26-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-26-ss-6-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "not",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Negative obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(6) A direction under this section is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "A direction under this section is an obligation that does not impose a duty."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-27",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "27 Directions—performance of functions or exercise of powers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-27"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "under laws of the Commonwealth\n\n(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing, give\ndirections to the following persons in relation to the performance\nof functions, or the exercise of powers, by those persons under a\nlaw of the Commonwealth:\n\n(a) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nDelegation and directions  Division 7\n\nSection 27\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the Migration\nAct 1958.\nNote:\nSection 499 of the Migration Act 1958 allows the Minister to give\ndirections to a person or body about the performance of functions or\nthe exercise of powers under that Act.\nCompliance with directions\n\n(3) A person mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) must comply with a\ndirection under this section.\nNote 1:\nSee subsection 13(4) and sections 15, 28 and 29 of the Public Service\nAct 1999 for the consequences of an APS employee in the Department\nnot complying with subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 2:\nSee section 57 of this Act for the termination of a person’s\nengagement as a consultant or contractor, or for the arranging of a\nperson to cease to perform services for the Department, if the person\ndoes not comply with subsection (3) of this section.\nDirections are not legislative instruments\n\n(4) A direction under this section is not a legislative instrument.\nNo limit on other powers to give directions\n\n(5) This section does not limit any other power of the Australian\nBorder Force Commissioner to give directions to any person.",
      "skos:definition": "under laws of the Commonwealth\n\n(1) The Australian Border Force Commissioner may, by writing, give\ndirections to the following persons in relation to the performance\nof functions, or the exercise of powers, by those persons under a\nlaw of the Commonwealth:\n\n(a) a person who is covered by paragraph (a) of the definition of\nImmigration and Border Protection worker in\nsubsection 4(1) and who is in the Australian Border Force;\n\n\nAustralian Border Force Commissioner  Part 2\nDelegation and directions  Division 7\n\nSection 27\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person who is covered by paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)\nof that definition and whose services are made available to,\nor who is performing services for, the Australian Border\nForce.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the Migration\nAct 1958.\nNote:\nSection 499 of the Migration Act 1958 allows the Minister to give\ndirections to a person or body about the performance of functions or\nthe exercise of powers under that Act.\nCompliance with directions\n\n(3) A person mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) must comply with a\ndirection under this section.\nNote 1:\nSee subsection 13(4) and sections 15, 28 and 29 of the Public Service\nAct 1999 for the consequences of an APS employee in the Department\nnot complying with subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 2:\nSee section 57 of this Act for the termination of a person’s\nengagement as a consultant or contractor, or for the arranging of a\nperson to cease to perform services for the Department, if the person\ndoes not comply with subsection (3) of this section.\nDirections are not legislative instruments\n\n(4) A direction under this section is not a legislative instrument.\nNo limit on other powers to give directions\n\n(5) This section does not limit any other power of the Australian\nBorder Force Commissioner to give directions to any person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-27-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-27-ss-2"
        },
