      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(3) This subsection applies if:\n\n(a) all of the following apply:\n\n\nAlcohol and drug tests  Part 5\n\nSection 36\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) the worker is an officer authorised to carry arms within\nthe meaning of section 189A of the Customs Act 1901;\n\n(ii) an incident occurs in which a person is killed or\nseriously injured as a result of the discharge of a firearm\nby the worker;\n\n(iii) the incident occurs in the course of the worker\nperforming his or her duties as an Immigration and\nBorder Protection worker; or\n\n(b) both of the following apply:\n\n(i) an incident occurs in which a person is killed or\nseriously injured as a result of the application of\nphysical force by the worker;\n\n(ii) the incident occurs in the course of the worker\nperforming his or her duties as an Immigration and\nBorder Protection worker.\nDirection to be given as soon as practicable after the incident",
      "skos:definition": "(3) This subsection applies if:\n\n(a) all of the following apply:\n\n\nAlcohol and drug tests  Part 5\n\nSection 36\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) the worker is an officer authorised to carry arms within\nthe meaning of section 189A of the Customs Act 1901;\n\n(ii) an incident occurs in which a person is killed or\nseriously injured as a result of the discharge of a firearm\nby the worker;\n\n(iii) the incident occurs in the course of the worker\nperforming his or her duties as an Immigration and\nBorder Protection worker; or\n\n(b) both of the following apply:\n\n(i) an incident occurs in which a person is killed or\nseriously injured as a result of the application of\nphysical force by the worker;\n\n(ii) the incident occurs in the course of the worker\nperforming his or her duties as an Immigration and\nBorder Protection worker.\nDirection to be given as soon as practicable after the incident",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bab5e45fc78c104f921c4e06bc8b4231ca1fef377eeec4bb13581c2609bc420d",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on using physical force in certain circumstances"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-36-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36(3) Alcohol screening, breath or blood test or prohibited drug test—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(3) This subsection applies if:\n\n(a) all of the following apply:\n\n\nAlcohol and drug tests  Part 5\n\nSection 36\n\nAustralian Border Force Act 2015\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) the worker is an officer authorised to carry arms within\nthe meaning of section 189A of the Customs Act 1901;\n\n(ii) an incident occurs in which a person is killed or\nseriously injured as a result of the discharge of a firearm\nby the worker;\n\n(iii) the incident occurs in the course of the worker\nperforming his or her duties as an Immigration and\nBorder Protection worker; or\n\n(b) both of the following apply:\n\n(i) an incident occurs in which a person is killed or\nseriously injured as a result of the application of\nphysical force by the worker;\n\n(ii) the incident occurs in the course of the worker\nperforming his or her duties as an Immigration and\nBorder Protection worker.\nDirection to be given as soon as practicable after the incident"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36-ss-3-norm",
