    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36(5) Alcohol screening, breath or blood test or prohibited drug test—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-36-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n\n(a) an Immigration and Border Protection worker is involved in\nan incident referred to in subsection (2) or (3); and\n\n(b) the worker attends or is admitted to a hospital for\nexamination or treatment because of the incident;\nan authorised person may give the worker a written direction\nrequiring the worker to do either or both of the following:\n\n(c) provide a sample of his or her blood for the purpose of an\nalcohol blood test;\n\n(d) provide a body sample of a kind specified in the direction for\na prohibited drug test.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If:\n\n(a) an Immigration and Border Protection worker is involved in\nan incident referred to in subsection (2) or (3); and\n\n(b) the worker attends or is admitted to a hospital for\nexamination or treatment because of the incident;\nan authorised person may give the worker a written direction\nrequiring the worker to do either or both of the following:\n\n(c) provide a sample of his or her blood for the purpose of an\nalcohol blood test;\n\n(d) provide a body sample of a kind specified in the direction for\na prohibited drug test.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f4207a4f9558aec8dab316266b62241e9a2478c45d1ea48fcd50c93292a4603e",
      "skos:note": "Worker must provide blood sample for alcohol test or prohibited drug test upon request.",
      "dc:description": "yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-36-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36(5) Alcohol screening, breath or blood test or prohibited drug test—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n\n(a) an Immigration and Border Protection worker is involved in\nan incident referred to in subsection (2) or (3); and\n\n(b) the worker attends or is admitted to a hospital for\nexamination or treatment because of the incident;\nan authorised person may give the worker a written direction\nrequiring the worker to do either or both of the following:\n\n(c) provide a sample of his or her blood for the purpose of an\nalcohol blood test;\n\n(d) provide a body sample of a kind specified in the direction for\na prohibited drug test."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-36-ss-5-norm",
