      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-42",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42 Secrecy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-42"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the person makes a record of, or discloses, information; and\n\n(c) the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(1A) If the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation because of the operation of subsection 4(5) or (6), the\nfault element of recklessness for paragraph (1)(c) of this section is\ntaken to be satisfied if the person is reckless as to whether or not\nwhichever of the following applies:\n\n(a) the information has a security classification;\n\n(b) the information originated with, or was received from, an\nintelligence agency;\n\n(c) the information was provided to the Commonwealth pursuant\nto a statutory obligation or otherwise by compulsion of law.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraph (1)(c)—see section 5.6\nof the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the person makes a record of, or discloses, information; and\n\n(c) the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(1A) If the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation because of the operation of subsection 4(5) or (6), the\nfault element of recklessness for paragraph (1)(c) of this section is\ntaken to be satisfied if the person is reckless as to whether or not\nwhichever of the following applies:\n\n(a) the information has a security classification;\n\n(b) the information originated with, or was received from, an\nintelligence agency;\n\n(c) the information was provided to the Commonwealth pursuant\nto a statutory obligation or otherwise by compulsion of law.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraph (1)(c)—see section 5.6\nof the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-42-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-42-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1c0ba1057a640bb7c899d2fe137d7bd83724e7d0ebffda10367c36faa8e2aae7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-42",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42 Secrecy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the person makes a record of, or discloses, information; and\n\n(c) the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(1A) If the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation because of the operation of subsection 4(5) or (6), the\nfault element of recklessness for paragraph (1)(c) of this section is\ntaken to be satisfied if the person is reckless as to whether or not\nwhichever of the following applies:\n\n(a) the information has a security classification;\n\n(b) the information originated with, or was received from, an\nintelligence agency;\n\n(c) the information was provided to the Commonwealth pursuant\nto a statutory obligation or otherwise by compulsion of law.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraph (1)(c)—see section 5.6\nof the Criminal Code."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-42-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42(1) Secrecy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-42-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the person makes a record of, or discloses, information; and\n\n(c) the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the person makes a record of, or discloses, information; and\n\n(c) the information is Immigration and Border Protection\ninformation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
