      "cml:premiseText": "(c) The making of the record, or disclosure, is for the purposes of an IGIS official exercising a power, or performing a function, or duty."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-44",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44 Disclosure to certain bodies and persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-44"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "Immigration and Border Protection information that is not\npersonal information\n\n(1) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that does not\ncontain personal information, to a body or person mentioned in\nsubsection (4) if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the\nfunctions, duties or powers of that body or person; and\n\n(b) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to\ncomply with a condition before the disclosure of the\ninformation—that body or person has complied with that\ncondition.\nImmigration and Border Protection information that is personal\ninformation\n\n(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that contains\npersonal information, to a body or person mentioned in\nsubsection (4) for a purpose mentioned in section 46 if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the\nfunctions, duties or powers of that body or person; and\n\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of the\ninformation to that body or person is necessary for the\npurpose mentioned in section 46; and\n\n(c) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to\ncomply with a condition before the disclosure of the\ninformation—that body or person has complied with that\ncondition.",
      "skos:definition": "Immigration and Border Protection information that is not\npersonal information\n\n(1) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that does not\ncontain personal information, to a body or person mentioned in\nsubsection (4) if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the\nfunctions, duties or powers of that body or person; and\n\n(b) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to\ncomply with a condition before the disclosure of the\ninformation—that body or person has complied with that\ncondition.\nImmigration and Border Protection information that is personal\ninformation\n\n(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that contains\npersonal information, to a body or person mentioned in\nsubsection (4) for a purpose mentioned in section 46 if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the\nfunctions, duties or powers of that body or person; and\n\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of the\ninformation to that body or person is necessary for the\npurpose mentioned in section 46; and\n\n(c) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to\ncomply with a condition before the disclosure of the\ninformation—that body or person has complied with that\ncondition.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-44-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-44-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8030713acc64d85531b43628af919cfc8b82d76a86807930edfe49dc33276dbc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-44",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44 Disclosure to certain bodies and persons",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "Immigration and Border Protection information that is not\npersonal information\n\n(1) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that does not\ncontain personal information, to a body or person mentioned in\nsubsection (4) if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the\nfunctions, duties or powers of that body or person; and\n\n(b) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to\ncomply with a condition before the disclosure of the\ninformation—that body or person has complied with that\ncondition.\nImmigration and Border Protection information that is personal\ninformation\n\n(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that contains\npersonal information, to a body or person mentioned in\nsubsection (4) for a purpose mentioned in section 46 if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist that body or person to perform or exercise any of the\nfunctions, duties or powers of that body or person; and\n\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of the\ninformation to that body or person is necessary for the\npurpose mentioned in section 46; and\n\n(c) if, under subsection (6), that body or person is required to\ncomply with a condition before the disclosure of the\ninformation—that body or person has complied with that\ncondition."
    },
