    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-45-ss-1-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Conditional",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conditional permission granted by Immigration and Border Protection.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will be used in accordance with an agreement to which subsection (4) applies;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-45-ss-1-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on further disclosure of Immigration and Border Protection information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) that foreign country, agency, authority or organisation has undertaken not to use or further disclose the information except in accordance with the agreement or otherwise as required or authorised by law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-45-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45(2) Disclosure in accordance with agreements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-45-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that contains\npersonal information, to a foreign country, an agency or authority\nof a foreign country or a public international organisation for a\npurpose mentioned in section 46 if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will be used in\naccordance with an agreement to which subsection (4)\napplies; and\n\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of that\ninformation to that foreign country, agency, authority or\norganisation is necessary for the purpose mentioned in\nsection 46; and\n\n(c) that foreign country, agency, authority or organisation has\nundertaken not to use or further disclose the information\nexcept in accordance with the agreement or otherwise as\nrequired or authorised by law.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that contains\npersonal information, to a foreign country, an agency or authority\nof a foreign country or a public international organisation for a\npurpose mentioned in section 46 if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will be used in\naccordance with an agreement to which subsection (4)\napplies; and\n\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of that\ninformation to that foreign country, agency, authority or\norganisation is necessary for the purpose mentioned in\nsection 46; and\n\n(c) that foreign country, agency, authority or organisation has\nundertaken not to use or further disclose the information\nexcept in accordance with the agreement or otherwise as\nrequired or authorised by law.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-45"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-45-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-45-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b949967b75b59ae3e23607df6c5b77a6083d849ff56b697a92cd8bc5b4304191",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of personal information to foreign countries, agencies, or organisations for a specific purpose."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-45-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45(2) Disclosure in accordance with agreements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "(2) An entrusted person authorised under subsection (3) may disclose\nImmigration and Border Protection information that contains\npersonal information, to a foreign country, an agency or authority\nof a foreign country or a public international organisation for a\npurpose mentioned in section 46 if:\n\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that the information will be used in\naccordance with an agreement to which subsection (4)\napplies; and\n\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that the disclosure of that\ninformation to that foreign country, agency, authority or\norganisation is necessary for the purpose mentioned in\nsection 46; and\n\n(c) that foreign country, agency, authority or organisation has\nundertaken not to use or further disclose the information\nexcept in accordance with the agreement or otherwise as\nrequired or authorised by law."
    },
    {
