    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 Interaction with Privacy Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988:\n\n(a) the making of a record, in accordance with section 43, of\nImmigration and Border Protection information, to the extent\nthat the Immigration and Border Protection information\ncontains personal information, is taken to be a use that is\nauthorised by this Act; and",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988:\n\n(a) the making of a record, in accordance with section 43, of\nImmigration and Border Protection information, to the extent\nthat the Immigration and Border Protection information\ncontains personal information, is taken to be a use that is\nauthorised by this Act; and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-51-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-51-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "440ca00320d570c25ee446168b5992416b3a2e6efcd84a1e2987bea9d96716dc",
      "skos:note": "Use of Immigration and Border Protection information is authorized for record-making purposes under the Privacy Act 1988."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 Interaction with Privacy Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988:\n\n(a) the making of a record, in accordance with section 43, of\nImmigration and Border Protection information, to the extent\nthat the Immigration and Border Protection information\ncontains personal information, is taken to be a use that is\nauthorised by this Act; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-51-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-51"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-51-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Authorisation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorization of use",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Section 43, Privacy Act 1988",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Use is authorized"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-52",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-52"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "•\nThe Secretary and the Comptroller-General of Customs can\ndelegate their functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth.\n•\nThe Secretary may give directions to Immigration and Border\nProtection workers to do with the administration and control\nof the Department or the performance of functions or exercise\nof powers by such workers under a law of the Commonwealth.\n•\nThe Secretary or the Australian Border Force Commissioner\nmay terminate the engagement of a person as a consultant or\ncontractor if the person fails to comply with a direction under\nthis Act.\n•\nThe Minister may make rules for the purposes of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nThe Secretary and the Comptroller-General of Customs can\ndelegate their functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth.\n•\nThe Secretary may give directions to Immigration and Border\nProtection workers to do with the administration and control\nof the Department or the performance of functions or exercise\nof powers by such workers under a law of the Commonwealth.\n•\nThe Secretary or the Australian Border Force Commissioner\nmay terminate the engagement of a person as a consultant or\ncontractor if the person fails to comply with a direction under\nthis Act.\n•\nThe Minister may make rules for the purposes of this Act.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-52-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-52-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5e0a972f997dec89ba0a0cb4594de843b55f85b8573f4a7480a22b738d5dc3cd",
      "skos:note": "Delegation of functions or powers under a law of the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-52",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "•\nThe Secretary and the Comptroller-General of Customs can\ndelegate their functions or powers under a law of the\nCommonwealth.\n•\nThe Secretary may give directions to Immigration and Border\nProtection workers to do with the administration and control\nof the Department or the performance of functions or exercise\nof powers by such workers under a law of the Commonwealth.\n•\nThe Secretary or the Australian Border Force Commissioner\nmay terminate the engagement of a person as a consultant or\ncontractor if the person fails to comply with a direction under\nthis Act.\n•\nThe Minister may make rules for the purposes of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-52-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-52"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-52-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "canDelegate",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Delegation of functions or powers",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Delegation by Secretary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-act-2015.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by writing, delegate any of his or her functions\nor powers under a law of the Commonwealth to:\n\n(a) the Australian Border Force Commissioner; or\n\n(b) an Immigration and Border Protection worker.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to:\n\n(a) section 30 (resignation in anticipation of termination of\nemployment); or\n\n(b) section 32 (termination of employment for serious\nmisconduct); or\n\n(c) the Migration Act 1958 or an instrument under that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, by writing, delegate any of his or her functions\nor powers under a law of the Commonwealth to:\n\n(a) the Australian Border Force Commissioner; or\n\n(b) an Immigration and Border Protection worker.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to:\n\n(a) section 30 (resignation in anticipation of termination of\nemployment); or\n\n(b) section 32 (termination of employment for serious\nmisconduct); or\n\n(c) the Migration Act 1958 or an instrument under that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-53-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-53-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5749a35621451025fc5ee1fcf982987bb600c79fc3089314015c916e75cfd216"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-act-2015#sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Delegation by Secretary",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by writing, delegate any of his or her functions\nor powers under a law of the Commonwealth to:\n\n(a) the Australian Border Force Commissioner; or\n\n(b) an Immigration and Border Protection worker.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to:\n\n(a) section 30 (resignation in anticipation of termination of\nemployment); or\n\n(b) section 32 (termination of employment for serious\nmisconduct); or\n\n(c) the Migration Act 1958 or an instrument under that Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-act-2015-sec-53-ss-1",
